{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-core":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-core/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-lichnerowicz-wkb-corollary","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Remark","doco:Section"],"label":"rem:lichnerowicz-wkb-corollary","kind":"remark","title":"Lichnerowicz identity reduces the $\\Phi_q$-WKB conjecture","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-categorical-lichnerowicz","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-categorical-instanton"],"interprets":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-categorical-lichnerowicz","tags":["lichnerowicz","q-laplacian","categorical-dirac","wkb"],"text":"lichnerowicz-wkb-corollary.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"rem:lichnerowicz-wkb-corollary\"></a><p>The categorical Lichnerowicz identity provides the gauge Hessian at the categorical-instanton saddle. This <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code>-Laplacian <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\Delta_\\nabla^q</code> equals <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathfrak{D}_\\nabla^2</code> on the parallel-Reeb background. The Pfaffian structure on chiral spinors converts <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">-\\tfrac{1}{2}\\log \\det \\Delta_\\nabla^q = -\\log \\det |\\mathfrak{D}_\\nabla| = -\\tfrac{1}{2}\\log \\det \\mathfrak{D}_\\nabla</code>, recovering the WKB <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">S_1</code> formula.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/lichnerowicz-wkb-corollary.md","heading":"Remark","number":"4.17.10","page":"b/rem-lichnerowicz-wkb-corollary","qa":{"counts":{"pass":57,"fail":1,"warn":1,"na":18,"unknown":0,"stale":0},"milnor":{"total":2,"notPassing":1}}}
